---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Privacy policy — Trivarone"
  description="What personal information trivarone.com collects, why, who else sees it, and how to have it corrected or deleted. Prepared in accordance with the Australian Privacy Principles."
  path="/privacy"
>
  <section class="titleblock">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="standfirst">
        What this website collects, why, and what happens to it. Prepared in accordance
        with the Australian Privacy Principles.
      </p>
      <p class="articlemeta">
        Last updated <time datetime="2026-09-06">6 September 2026</time>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="lede">
          Trivarone is a sole trader business based in Brisbane, Australia, owned and
          operated by Pradeep Anandraj. ABN 65 502 768 472.
        </p>

        <h2>What is collected</h2>

        <p>
          If you use the <a href="/contact">contact form</a>, Trivarone collects your
          name, email address, business name, and whatever you write in the message.
        </p>

        <p>
          If you request the <a href="/check">free discoverability check</a>,
          Trivarone collects your business name, website address, the service you offer,
          your suburb and your email address. Your name and a note are optional.
        </p>

        <p>
          If you email or telephone directly, Trivarone holds whatever you choose to
          provide.
        </p>

        <p>
          Nothing on this website requires you to create an account, and no payment
          information is collected here.
        </p>

        <h2>Information collected automatically</h2>

        <p>
          Like most websites, this one records technical information when a page is
          requested: the pages viewed, the approximate location, the browser and device
          used, and the site you arrived from.
        </p>

        <p>
          Trivarone uses Microsoft Clarity to understand how visitors use the site.
          Clarity records page interactions, which can include mouse movement, scrolling
          and clicks, and produces anonymised session recordings and heatmaps. It masks
          form fields and does not capture what you type into them. Microsoft states that
          this information is not used to train its models.
        </p>

        <h2>Why it is collected</h2>

        <p>
          To respond to your enquiry. To carry out work you have asked for. To understand
          which parts of the site are useful and which are not.
        </p>

        <p>
          Nothing collected here is used for advertising, and nothing is sold.
        </p>

        <h2>Who else sees it</h2>

        <p>
          Trivarone uses services based outside Australia, which means information passes
          to them.
        </p>

        <ul class="plainlist">
          <li><strong>Formspree</strong> (United States) — processes form submissions, retains a copy, and forwards them by email</li>
          <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> (United States) — hosts this website and holds server logs</li>
          <li><strong>Microsoft</strong> (United States) — provides Clarity analytics and the email service used to reply to you</li>
          <li><strong>HubSpot</strong> (United States) — holds contact records for people Trivarone is in ongoing conversation with</li>
        </ul>

        <p>
          Trivarone does not sell personal information, and does not share it with anyone
          beyond the services listed above.
        </p>

        <h2>How long it is kept</h2>

        <p>
          Enquiries are kept while the conversation is active, and for a reasonable period
          afterwards in case you get back in touch. Contact records are kept while the
          relationship continues. Clarity session data is retained for 90 days.
        </p>

        <h2>Access, correction and deletion</h2>

        <p>
          You may ask what Trivarone holds about you, ask for it to be corrected, or ask
          for it to be deleted. Email
          <a href="mailto:pradeep@trivarone.com">pradeep@trivarone.com</a> and you will
          have a reply within five working days.
        </p>

        <h2>Complaints</h2>

        <p>
          If you have a concern about how your information has been handled, email
          <a href="mailto:pradeep@trivarone.com">pradeep@trivarone.com</a> and it will be
          looked into properly. You can also raise privacy concerns with the Office of the
          Australian Information Commissioner at
          <a href="https://www.oaic.gov.au" rel="noopener">oaic.gov.au</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>

        <p>
          If this policy changes, the date at the top changes with it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band band--navy">
    <div class="shell">
      <h2>Any questions about this, just ask.</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="lede">
          If anything here is unclear, or you would like to know exactly what is held
          about you, send an email and you will get a straight answer.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="btn" href="/contact">Start a conversation</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
